{
  "id": "grammar.a2.11.03.preguntas",
  "title": "Questions in the Pretérito Indefinido",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "To ask about completed past events, use a question word followed by the pretérito indefinido form. Answers use the same tense. Common questions include ¿*Qué* *hiciste*?, ¿*Dónde* *estuviste*?, ¿Qué *compraste*? and ¿Fuiste al concierto?"
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "¿Qué hiciste ayer?",
          "english": "What did you do yesterday?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "¿Dónde estuviste?",
          "english": "Where were you?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "¿Qué compraste?",
          "english": "What did you buy?"
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Fui al festival.",
          "english": "I went to the festival."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        [
          "¿qué hiciste?",
          "what did you do?"
        ],
        [
          "¿dónde estuviste?",
          "where were you?"
        ],
        [
          "¿qué compraste?",
          "what did you buy?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Use the pretérito indefinido for completed past actions. Watch the irregular forms carefully because they do not follow the regular endings."
    },
